/target
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock IS committed, deliberately. The old advice not to commit it for a
# library is out of date: it is ignored by downstream consumers either way, and
# committing it makes CI reproducible, lets `cargo audit` see exact versions, and
# makes the declared MSRV mean something -- without it, dependencies resolve to
# whatever is newest and the floor moves on its own.
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.so
*.pyd
.venv/
dist/

# Node addon build output and dependencies
node_modules/
*.node
hivecomb-node/index.js
hivecomb-node/index.d.ts
package-lock.json

# Secrets. Nothing holding a private key may ever be committed — this repo is
# about to be public, and git history keeps what you delete.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.wif
wallet.json
